---
// The curves the collection is missing: the named classical curves the generators already
// know, and the crossing x inflection cells with no curve at all.
// Spec: state/SPEC-extra-curves-int.md. Data: app/src/data/extra-curves.json.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import gaps from "../data/extra-curves.json";
import { existsSync } from "node:fs";
import { fileURLToPath } from "node:url";

// the figures are written by scripts/extra_curve_figs.py; a card with no figure just has none
const FIGURES = fileURLToPath(new URL("../../public/extra-curves/", import.meta.url));
const slugOf = (key) => key.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, "-").replace(/^-|-$/g, "");

const { missingNamed, emptyCells, familiesWithoutRating, count, addedOnRequest = [] } = gaps;
const cellsByCrossings = new Map();
for (const cell of emptyCells) {
  if (!cellsByCrossings.has(cell.crossings)) cellsByCrossings.set(cell.crossings, []);
  cellsByCrossings.get(cell.crossings).push(cell.inflections);
}
---

<BaseLayout title="extra curves" pageTitle="Extra curves">
  <p class="lead">What the collection of {count.curves} curves does not have: named classical
    curves whose equations are already written in the generators, and the crossing ×
    inflection cells with no curve at all. Nothing here is created by visiting it; this page is
    the shopping list. The Tschirnhausen family at the top is the one proposal already made
    real.</p>

  {addedOnRequest.length > 0 && (
    <>
      <h2>Added on request · Tschirnhausen</h2>
      <p class="note">This family was proposed here and has since been created. The plates are
        the collection's own, side curves and all; the equation is
        <code>x = t² − 3, y = t(t² − 3)</code>, and the node sits at t = ±√3, so the crossing
        point has no rational parameter and the records are sampled.</p>
      <div class="gaps">
        {addedOnRequest.map((curve) => (
          <article class="gap">
            <a href={`/tune/${curve.uid}`} title="open the tuning page">
              <img class="thumb" src={`/api/print-plate/${curve.uid}?format=svg`}
                alt={curve.name} loading="lazy" />
            </a>
            <h3>{curve.name}</h3>
            <p class="tag">{curve.uid} · in the collection</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </>
  )}

  <h2>Named classical curves not in the collection · {count.missingNamed}</h2>
  <p class="note">Each equation already exists in <code>scripts/generators.py</code>, so a
    record is data entry and a figure, not new mathematics. The <em>shape</em> line is the
    generator's own one-line description.</p>
  <p class="note">Each figure shows the proposed curve in black with its <b>side curves</b> in
    ochre, at a 2 % gap: the same law the plates use — outside at the ask, inside capped where
    it would fold at 0.9 / κ. The stations are sampled from the equation, so the sides are a
    drawing of what the plate would do, not a record.</p>
  <div class="gaps">
    {missingNamed.map((curve) => (
      <article class="gap">
        {existsSync(`${FIGURES}${slugOf(curve.key)}.svg`) ? (
          <img class="thumb" src={`/extra-curves/${slugOf(curve.key)}.svg`}
            alt={`the ${curve.key} curve`} loading="lazy" />
        ) : (
          <p class="nofig">
            {["heart", "squircle"].includes(curve.key)
              ? "no figure yet — not rational, so it cannot join the exact set"
              : "no figure yet — built from the n / h / u / v form, not the branch table"}
          </p>
        )}
        <h3>{curve.key}</h3>
        <p class="eq"><code>{curve.eq}</code></p>
        <p class="shape">{curve.tail}</p>
        <p class="tag">degree {curve.deg || "—"}</p>
        {curve.key === "squircle" && (
          <p class="variants">
            fitted:{" "}
            <a href="/extra-curves/squircle-4-span.svg">4 spans · miss 0.53 %</a>{" · "}
            <a href="/extra-curves/squircle-8-span.svg">8 spans · miss 0.12 %</a>
            {" "}of the radius
          </p>
        )}
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2>Loop ends · append a loop to a leg</h2>
  <p class="note">A curve like Tschirnhausen ends in a loop. These are the family
    <code>x = t² − c, y = t(t² − c)</code>: <code>c</code> sets the loop's size, the tail stays
    the same shape. The slider turns the loop to the leg's angle — a rotation changes a
    tangent's direction and never its length, so the join is exact at every angle. Set the
    slider to the angle a leg leaves at and the loop continues it without a kink.</p>
  <div class="loop-lab">
    <div id="loop-preview" class="loop-preview"></div>
    <div class="loop-controls">
      <label>leg angle <input id="loop-angle" type="range" min="-90" max="90" step="0.5" value="60" />
        <output id="loop-angle-out">60.0°</output></label>
      <label>loop size <input id="loop-size" type="range" min="0.3" max="2" step="0.05" value="1" />
        <output id="loop-size-out">1.00×</output></label>
      <label>tail <input id="loop-tail" type="range" min="0.2" max="3" step="0.05" value="1" />
        <output id="loop-tail-out">1.00</output></label>
      <label>or type the angle <input id="loop-angle-type" type="number" min="-90" max="90" step="0.5" value="60" />
        <button type="button" id="loop-apply">set</button></label>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="gaps">
    {["loop-end-small", "loop-end", "loop-end-large", "loop-end-mirror"].map((slug) => (
      <article class="gap">
        <img class="thumb" src={`/extra-curves/${slug}.svg`} alt={slug} loading="lazy" />
        <h3>{slug}</h3>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2>The empty crossing × inflection cells · {count.emptyCells}</h2>
  <p class="note">A <b>crossing pair</b> is two parameters t₁ &lt; t₂ where the stroke passes
    through the same place (three passes through one point count as three pairs). An
    <b>inflection</b> is a station where the curve stops bending one way and starts bending the
    other. The pair of counts is a shape signature: every curve has one, and two curves with the
    same pair still differ in shape. Each row lists the inflection counts with no curve at that
    many crossing pairs.</p>
  <p class="note"><b>Measured curves only.</b> The table counts the 262 curves with a recorded
    exact measurement. The 158 stored paths have no exact crossing or inflection count yet, so
    they are not in it — a cell can be empty here and still be occupied by a path that has not
    been measured. Read it as "no measured curve", not "no curve".</p>
  <table class="cells">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>crossing pairs</th><th>inflections with no curve</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {[...cellsByCrossings.entries()].sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0]).map(([crossings, list]) => (
        <tr><td>{crossings}</td><td>{list.sort((a, b) => a - b).join(", ")}</td></tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Families with no curve rated 2/10 or more</h2>
  <p class="note">These exist in the collection but have never been chosen; a family that is
    never chosen is a family the operator has not yet seen at its best.</p>
  <ul class="families">
    {familiesWithoutRating.map((row) => (
      <li><b>{row.family}</b> · {row.curves} curve(s)</li>
    ))}
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  import { mount } from "../scripts/loop-join.js";

  const host = document.getElementById("loop-preview");
  const controls = {
    angle: document.getElementById("loop-angle"),
    size: document.getElementById("loop-size"),
    tail: document.getElementById("loop-tail"),
    angleOut: document.getElementById("loop-angle-out"),
    sizeOut: document.getElementById("loop-size-out"),
    tailOut: document.getElementById("loop-tail-out"),
  };
  const lab = mount(host, controls);
  const typed = document.getElementById("loop-angle-type");
  document.getElementById("loop-apply").addEventListener("click", () => {
    const value = Number(typed.value);
    if (!Number.isFinite(value)) return;
    controls.angle.value = String(Math.max(-90, Math.min(90, value)));
    lab.repaint();
  });
</script>

<style is:global>
  .lead { font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6; color: #3c352c; max-width: 70ch; }
  .note { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: #6b5d49; max-width: 70ch; }
  .gaps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 14px; margin: 14px 0 28px; }
  .gap { margin: 0; padding: 10px 12px; background: #fffef9; border: 1px solid #eee3d3; }
  .gap h3 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 15px; }
  .gap .eq { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; word-break: break-word; }
  .gap .shape { margin: 0; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.5; color: #5a4a36; }
  .gap .tag { margin: 6px 0 0; font: 11px/1.4 ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; color: #8a6a1f; }
  .gap .thumb { display: block; width: 100%; height: 150px; object-fit: contain; background: #fff; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .gap .variants { margin: 6px 0 0; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.5; color: #5a4a36; }
  .gap .variants a { color: #7a5a1f; }
  .gap .nofig { margin: 0 0 8px; height: 150px; display: grid; place-items: center; text-align: center;
    font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.5; color: #8a7a62; background: #faf7f0; border: 1px dashed #e6dccb; padding: 8px; }
  .cells { border-collapse: collapse; font: 13px/1.5 ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; margin: 10px 0 26px; }
  .cells th, .cells td { padding: 4px 14px 4px 0; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee3d3; }
  .families { columns: 2; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; }
  .loop-lab { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 240px; gap: 16px; align-items: start; margin: 12px 0 18px; }
  .loop-preview { border: 1px solid #e6dccb; background: #fff; }
  .loop-preview svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .loop-controls { display: grid; gap: 8px; font: 12px/1.4 ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; }
  .loop-controls label { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 6.5rem minmax(0, 1fr) 3rem; gap: 6px; align-items: center; }
  .loop-controls label:nth-child(4) { grid-template-columns: 6.5rem 4rem auto; }
  .loop-controls button { padding: 2px 10px; white-space: nowrap; }
  .loop-controls input[type="range"] { width: 100%; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .loop-lab { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
</style>
